      "updated_at": "2025-10-08T11:16:01Z",
      "body": "I found the issue. It's a broader issue with Argument Clinic and how we handle exit paths for `PyUNicode_FSDecoder`:\n\n```c\nstatic PyObject *\nbuiltin_compile(PyObject *module, PyObject *const *args, Py_ssize_t nargs, PyObject *kwnames)\n{\n...\n    if (!PyUnicode_FSDecoder(args[1], &filename)) {\n        goto exit;\n    }\n...\n    if (args[5]) {\n        optimize = PyLong_AsInt(args[5]);\n        if (optimize == -1 && PyErr_Occurred()) {\n            goto exit;\n        }\n        if (!--noptargs) {\n            goto skip_optional_pos;\n        }\n    }\n...\nexit:\n    return return_value;\n}\n```\n\nWhen `PyUnicode_FSDecoder` is successful, it sets `filename` to a strong reference of the decoded string. However, in the above code, if `args[5]` (that is, `optimize`) fails to be converted, we don't decref that converted value.\n\nThe reason why we don't have a leak for successful paths is because we do `Py_DECREF(filename);` in `builtin_compile_impl` but that fix is incorrect. It only handles paths where AC was successful in the conversion, but leaves error ones with a leak.",
      "author_association": "MEMBER",
      "pin": null,
