      "created_at": "2025-10-08T11:18:16Z",
      "updated_at": "2025-10-08T11:25:10Z",
      "body": "The regression was never caught because when we moved `compile` to Argument Clinic, it was likely forgotten to remove the `Py_DECREF`. If it was removed, there would be a leak, but maybe it went unnoticed. This more directly affet `_symtable.symtable`. In other words: don't use `PyUnicode_FSDecode` or other converters that set a strong reference to a PyObject* as the conversion result. Wrap them using a true AC converter with a cleanup.",
      "author_association": "MEMBER",
      "pin": null,
