      "created_at": "2025-10-08T13:50:39Z",
      "updated_at": "2025-10-08T14:19:05Z",
      "body": "More generally, there is a deeper issue when using `object` + a custom converter in Argument Clinic with a target type `PyObject *`. If the function admits more arguments *after*, then a cleanup step for the converted object must always exist, otherwise we will have a leak.\n\nEDIT: The `_conversion_converter` converter for Interpolation is fine because it actually uses a borrowed reference instead.",
